From e360c6a101df1601480e602b0b99812e311d7fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:11:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 090/118] rule-set: refuse what cannot be a rule-set before
 reading it, say what came

A 200 body was read whole, up to the 50 MB cap, before its size and format
were looked at. Refuse a declared length above the cap, and for the binary
format a body without the magic bytes, before reading; read into a slice
sized by the declared length.

A body that does not parse now reports its size, Content-Type and first
bytes (quoted, cut), so that an error page is told from a damaged file.

An update cut by the shutdown is no longer logged or counted as a failed
update, and the stall timer stops when the transfer ends.
---
 route/rule/rule_set_remote.go           |  89 ++++++++++++++--
 route/rule/rule_set_remote_body_test.go | 132 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 214 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 route/rule/rule_set_remote_body_test.go

diff --git a/route/rule/rule_set_remote.go b/route/rule/rule_set_remote.go
